y bit order. The period check counts busy cycles, which are unaffected by data or parity values. Not done: VeriTriage was not rerun on each log individually, and the failures were not rerun to rule out flakiness. Both remain open."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/repro_data_byte.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro A: data bits must be sent LSB first", "summary": "Self-checking repro for bucket A against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. It sends the non-palindromic bytes 01, 80, C5 and 12, samples each of the eight data bits mid-bit, and compares the sampled byte with the byte sent. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish. Serves [requirement:req-94eee275db].", "entry": "tb_uart_repro"}, {"path": "tb/repro_parity_bit.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro B: parity bit must be even parity", "summary": "Self-checking repro for bucket B against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. It sends bytes 00, 01, 03, 07, FF and B4, samples the parity bit mid-bit, and compares it with ^data, which does not depend on bit order. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish. Serves [requirement:req-94eee275db].", "entry": "tb_uart_repro"}, {"path": "tb/repro_frame_period.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro C: frame must last 11 bit periods", "summary": "Self-checking repro for bucket C against [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. For two frames it counts the clock cycles while busy is high and expects 11*CLKS_PER_BIT = 44. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the nonce before $finish. Serves [requirement:req-94eee275db].", "entry": "tb_uart_repro"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001"], "claims": ["By reading the RTL, I expect each repro to fail on uart_frame_tx_buggy.v. This has not been simulated by me; the platform's simulator.run gate decides it.", "I expect each repro to pass on a corrected design with the same start-bit timing, LSB-first data, even parity